Summary of the build:
- **Title:** *"When 'Never' Needs an Exit Code"* (retitled from *"The Hook That Cannot Be Talked Out Of"* after GATE T §8.9 flagged "Of" as mid-word truncation).
- **Angle** — distinct from the sibling reel `cc-hook-advisory-vs-deterministic` built earlier tonight: the mechanism as a receipt. Advisory holds and leaves no artifact; the hook fires and leaves an exit code the OS honors, every call.
- **Session evidence** (`SESSION.md` + `evidence/`): two fresh headless `claude -p` runs on 2026-09-10 (Claude Code 2.1.150) + a direct hook payload demo. Run 1 (advisory-only): Claude refused in one text turn, no Write. Run 2 (hook active, CLAUDE.md moved fully out of `scratch/`): Claude wrote `Suggested letter grade: A-`, the tool_result came back `is_error` with the guard's block message verbatim, Claude read the guard, rewrote clean.
- **Final gate roster:** F, L, BANNED-CARD, SWEEP-WARN, G, V (28 frames, 0/0/0), T, SHARPNESS, BOOKEND, AUDIO, MASTER, LOUDNESS, RECEIPTS — all PASS.
- **Cost:** $0.587 total for the two Claude API calls; Kokoro/local for audio; no Higgsfield/ElevenLabs.
- **Not published.** Master stays in the reel folder.

